      "facts": [
        "Descriptive placement ids (COD-1043): `[<Screen>-]<Position>-<App>`, e.g. `Above-Input-Desktop`, `Inline-After-Agent-CLI`. `Legacy-` marks the old project agent chat on freebuff.com. The app is one of Desktop, CLI, Web, Mobile (the phone layout of freebuff.com), Android or iOS.",
        "The first canonical names (PR 9213), live 2026-11-01 for a few hours before the names above replaced them. Rows written in that window and the Gravity placements registered under them carry these, so they stay aliases.",
        "The canonical id for any id: a legacy or retired id maps to its new name, anything else is itself.",
        "Whether `id` is an old name (legacy or retired) for a renamed placement.",
        "Lazily fill a four-ad pool, then repeat it for later transcript slots. Canonical ids (COD-1043; legacy `CLI-Chat-Inline`, `Single-Ad-Unit-1`): the server maps them to the registered Gravity slugs.",
        "Keep the rotating above-input slot separate for reporting continuity."
      ],
